From 7a5c3a3565ffe56795d48bacce26e5251eb805dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satya Benson <satya@benson.earth>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:25:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] kboot: admit the J615 on the 25G83 profile behind an
 explicit opt-in

Apple's macOS 26.6.2 (25G83) restore image gives the J613 and the J615
one DCP image, one PMP image and one GPU image, and the J615's ADT dcp,
disp0, pmp, sgx and gfx-asc nodes equal the J613's but for phandles
(display clock IDs 345/416, same DCP firmware UUID C042E95C-...-6FDD).
Let the 25G83 path take a J615, experimentally:

- payload_profile_rank() ranks a J615 25G83 tree like the J613's on a
  26.6.2 boot. Selecting it hands nothing over by itself.
- The 25G83 display handoff (dcp_soc_j613_25g83) and GPU handoff
  (dt_set_gpu_t8122_26) take a J613 as before, and a J615 only with
  chosen.asahi,j615-25g83-experimental=1 (t8122_25g83_board()). Without
  it the J615 keeps the boot framebuffer and the GPU memory is only
  reserved, as on any refused handoff.

Every other gate (OS firmware 26.6.2, pinned DCP UUID, ADT clock IDs,
DART and segment checks, GPU ADT regions, asahi,t8122-gpu=1) is
unchanged. Not booted on a J615.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
